	(text "RS232 on ESP32 UART2 (GPIO32 TX, GPIO34 RX, on the module side that faces this port): replaces the 3.3 V TTL port.\nThe GPS port (GPIO16 / GPIO17) still shares UART2 through the GPIO matrix.\nU1101 MAX13223E: TOUT and RIN survive +/-70 V, so a pin wired to a 12/24 V vehicle supply or shorted to a J1 neighbour is not damaged.\nSupply 3.3 V. Charge pump at 3.0-3.6 V: C1-C3 = 0.1 uF, C4 (V-) = 1 uF, VCC bypass 0.1 uF (datasheet table 3). 250 kbps max.\nAlways on: FORCEON = FORCEOFF = 3.3 V, EN = GND (receivers enabled). AutoShutdown is not used: it would turn the driver off\nwhen the other device does not drive our RX. Channel 2 unused: T2IN tied to GND, R2IN/R2OUT/T2OUT and INVALID open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 40.64 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
